---
import Controls from './Controls.astro';
---
<figure class="placement-figure wide" data-placement-purchase aria-labelledby="placement-purchase-title">
  <figcaption id="placement-purchase-title"><span>Figure 3</span> <strong>Follow the purchase’s required owners</strong></figcaption>
  <div class="placement-panel">
    <div class="placement-options"><label><input type="checkbox" data-global /> Add hypothetical global order-ID owner G</label></div>
    <div class="placement-origin">North application · create Mina’s purchase 103</div>
    <div class="placement-owner-list">
      <div class="placement-owner" data-owner="A"><b>① A · leader North</b><p>Pending order 103 + lines</p><code>P7 × 1 · 20.00<br />P3 × 2 · 4.50</code><small>Total 29.00 · no payment</small><div class="placement-votes">A_N · A_W · A_E <span>Majority 2 of 3</span></div><strong data-owner-state data-live>Not yet counted</strong></div>
      <div class="placement-link" data-owner-link="P">A ⇄ P · North ⇄ West<br /><span>Coordinate stock work</span></div>
      <div class="placement-owner" data-owner="P"><b>② P · leader West</b><p>Guard both stock decrements</p><code>P7: 1 → 0<br />P3: 12 → 10</code><small>Shared product authority</small><div class="placement-votes">P_N · P_W · P_E <span>Majority 2 of 3</span></div><strong data-owner-state data-live>Not yet counted</strong></div>
      <div class="placement-link" data-global-only hidden>Purchase ⇄ G · East<br /><span>Enforce global ID association</span></div>
      <div class="placement-owner" data-owner="G" data-global-only hidden><b>③ G · leader East</b><p>Global order-ID association</p><code>103 → Mina’s order on A</code><small>Hypothetical enforcement owner</small><div class="placement-votes">G_N · G_W · G_E <span>Majority 2 of 3</span></div><strong data-owner-state data-live>Not yet counted</strong></div>
    </div>
    <p class="placement-result" data-dependencies data-live>Required data owners: A and P</p>
    <p class="placement-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The request originates in North. That places the application near A’s leader, not near every required owner.</p>
    <Controls label="Figure 3 controls" />
  </div>
  <p class="placement-caption">An independent replay from before purchase 103. Every displayed owner has one voter in North, West and East. Arrows identify required communication, not message order or a complete atomic-commit protocol. The full purchase needs one recoverable outcome across its participants; no partial purchase is shown as committed.</p>
  <details><summary>Purchase dependencies as text</summary><ol>
    <li>The North application reaches A’s leader in North.</li><li>A creates the order work. Its three-region group needs two voters.</li><li>The purchase also needs P’s stock authority in West. P’s three-region group separately needs two voters.</li><li>With G enabled, global uniqueness adds an owner led in East, with its own majority requirement. A, P and G must participate in the complete transaction protocol.</li><li>After any failure, every required owner and the joint transaction decision must remain reachable through a valid protocol. Local order rows alone do not complete the purchase.</li>
  </ol></details>
</figure>
<script>
  import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-placement-purchase]').forEach(root=>{
    const global=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-global]')!;
    const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>5,draw:(step:number)=>{
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-global-only]').forEach(el=>el.hidden=!global.checked);
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-owner]').forEach(el=>{
        const owner=el.dataset.owner!;
        const active=step>=(owner==='A'?1:owner==='P'?2:3);
        el.classList.toggle('is-active',active);
        el.querySelector('[data-owner-state]')!.textContent=active?'Required · own quorum path':'Not yet counted';
      });
      root.querySelector('[data-dependencies]')!.textContent=global.checked?'Required owners: A + P + G · each needs its own majority':'Required data owners: A + P · each needs its own majority';
      root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=[
        'The request originates in North. That places the application near A’s leader, not near every required owner.',
        'A owns Mina’s order and line work. A’s leader is local, but its voting group still spans three regions and needs two voters.',
        'P owns both stock rows. The purchase crosses to West for guarded decrements, and P separately needs agreement among its copies.',
        global.checked?'The hypothetical G in East governs the global order-ID association. It adds a required owner and a separate quorum path to the complete purchase protocol.':'A and P are the two data owners. Additional uniqueness, reference or index work must still be checked before calling this the complete participant set.',
        global.checked?'A, P and G must all have a usable path, and the atomic decision must remain recoverable. A surviving A alone cannot finish this purchase.':'Both A and P must have usable paths, and the atomic decision must remain recoverable. A local order does not make its stock purchase local.',
      ][step];
    }});
    global.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
  });
</script>
